Package: homelab-pgbouncer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pgbouncer
Recommends: homelab-database
Description: PgBouncer connection pooler in front of the shared homelab database
 Configures PgBouncer (scram-sha-256 auth, a static userlist.txt) with a
 `homelab` database entry pointing at a homelab-database-managed Postgres
 backend, local or remote. Config is a single drop-in file activated via
 pgbouncer's own native %include directive -- never hand-edits
 pgbouncer.ini beyond that one line. Ships
 scripts/bootstrap-pgbouncer-entry.sh, a reusable tool other homelab-*
 packages' installers call to register a role's SCRAM secret (from
 homelab-database's bootstrap-app-role.sh) into userlist.txt -- locally,
 over SSH to a remote pgbouncer host, or by printing the exact line for a
 human to add by hand -- never a stored/network admin credential.
 Every homelab-* app should connect through this pooler for normal
 runtime traffic; direct Postgres access is reserved for one-time
 role/schema bootstrap only.
